1
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:08,950
"Hoshimi Productions"

2
00:00:10,750 --> 00:00:12,620
My heart is beating so fast.

3
00:00:12,620 --> 00:00:14,950
There must be something...

4
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:23,830
Are you okay?

5
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:26,700
Thanks...

6
00:00:34,120 --> 00:00:37,290
She seemed really cool...

7
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:39,660
"Hoshimi Productions"

8
00:00:45,160 --> 00:00:47,290
Thank you very much!

9
00:00:52,620 --> 00:00:55,330
All right next, #4...

10
00:00:55,330 --> 00:00:56,410
Huh?!

11
00:00:56,410 --> 00:00:57,540
Yes.

12
00:00:57,540 --> 00:00:59,870
I'm #4, Kotono Nagase.

13
00:00:59,870 --> 00:01:01,250
Nagase...?

14
00:01:02,290 --> 00:01:03,540
H-Hey!

15
00:01:07,160 --> 00:01:09,120
All right, come on in.

16
00:01:11,540 --> 00:01:15,160
Kotono Nagase... By any chance...

17
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:17,500
I'm Mana Nagase's sister.

18
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:19,160
Mana's...?

19
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:23,080
What's the matter?

20
00:01:23,080 --> 00:01:24,370
Nothing.

21
00:01:24,370 --> 00:01:27,370
You're Mr. Shinji Saegusa, right?

22
00:01:27,370 --> 00:01:30,450
You managed my sister from the beginning.

23
00:01:30,450 --> 00:01:32,160
So what?

24
00:01:32,160 --> 00:01:35,330
Please guide me as you did her.

25
00:01:35,330 --> 00:01:38,500
I'm determined to make it through
any harsh training.

26
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:42,370
For this audition, I'm leaving
everything up to this guy.

27
00:01:42,370 --> 00:01:44,040
I'm Kohei Makino.

28
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:46,750
I'll be in charge if you pass the audition.

29
00:01:47,910 --> 00:01:51,080
You won't be in charge, Mr. Saegusa?

30
00:01:51,080 --> 00:01:54,000
Of course we'll take care of you as the agency.

31
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:57,120
But Makino will be your direct manager.

32
00:01:59,290 --> 00:02:01,450
First, let me ask you this:

33
00:02:01,450 --> 00:02:04,370
Why do you want to become an idol?

34
00:02:04,370 --> 00:02:07,450
I'm Mana Nagase's sister.

35
00:02:07,450 --> 00:02:10,450
Isn't that enough of a reason?

36
00:02:10,450 --> 00:02:13,700
I want to stand at the top of the Venus Program.

37
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:15,910
That's my goal.

38
00:03:49,910 --> 00:03:51,540
"Singing"
"Script Reading"

39
00:03:49,910 --> 00:03:51,540
Thank you very much.

40
00:03:51,540 --> 00:03:52,830
"Posing"
"Dancing"

41
00:03:51,540 --> 00:03:52,830
Have a seat.

42
00:03:58,830 --> 00:04:03,410
I'll judge you on how you judge the auditioners!

43
00:04:06,290 --> 00:04:08,910
All right next, #4...

44
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:11,250
Yes.

45
00:04:11,250 --> 00:04:13,750
I'm #4, Kotono Nagase.

46
00:04:13,750 --> 00:04:16,080
Nagase...?

47
00:04:16,080 --> 00:04:17,950
H-Hey!

48
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:21,580
Why would she leave?

49
00:04:22,580 --> 00:04:24,580
What's going on?

50
00:04:24,580 --> 00:04:26,120
It's nothing...

51
00:04:26,120 --> 00:04:30,080
If you pass, we'll have you
move into the company dorms.

52
00:04:30,080 --> 00:04:31,330
Is that all right?

53
00:04:31,330 --> 00:04:34,080
I'm able to commute from home.

54
00:04:34,080 --> 00:04:36,160
It's our policy.

55
00:04:36,160 --> 00:04:39,580
We want you to utilize what you gain
from living with other members

56
00:04:39,580 --> 00:04:42,700
and deepening your understanding
for each other.

57
00:04:42,700 --> 00:04:43,830
Members?

58
00:04:43,830 --> 00:04:44,370
"Hoshimi Productions
Newcomer Discovery Project"

59
00:04:44,370 --> 00:04:48,660
"Hoshimi Productions
Newcomer Discovery Project"

60
00:04:44,370 --> 00:04:48,660
We're thinking of forming a group
for this upcoming project.

61
00:04:48,660 --> 00:04:50,620
My sister was a solo artist.

62
00:04:51,910 --> 00:04:56,870
My sister made it all the way to the
Next Venus Grand Prix finals by herself.

63
00:04:56,870 --> 00:04:59,160
I'd like to be a solo artist, too.

64
00:04:59,160 --> 00:05:00,910
You're...

65
00:05:00,910 --> 00:05:02,450
I see.

66
00:05:02,450 --> 00:05:06,500
Still, I don't plan to change
anything about this project.

67
00:05:06,500 --> 00:05:08,000
If you can't agree to the terms,

68
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:12,250
you're more than welcome to pull out
before the results come in.

69
00:05:12,250 --> 00:05:14,540
This concludes today's audition.

70
00:05:14,540 --> 00:05:17,750
The results will be mailed out at a later date.

71
00:05:17,750 --> 00:05:19,790
Do you have any questions for me?

72
00:05:21,870 --> 00:05:23,370
I don't.

73
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:28,950
Excuse me...

74
00:05:28,950 --> 00:05:30,700
Miss Haruko, what is it?

75
00:05:30,700 --> 00:05:32,080
Wow!

76
00:05:32,080 --> 00:05:33,540
Is this a studio?

77
00:05:33,540 --> 00:05:34,910
Who is this?

78
00:05:34,910 --> 00:05:39,580
She just came into our office,
so I assumed she was an auditioner...

79
00:05:39,580 --> 00:05:42,620
She's the last one for the morning half.

80
00:05:42,620 --> 00:05:44,500
What's your number?

81
00:05:44,500 --> 00:05:45,870
My number?

82
00:05:45,870 --> 00:05:48,500
Where am I right now?

83
00:05:48,500 --> 00:05:50,750
We're a talent agency.

84
00:05:50,750 --> 00:05:52,500
Talent...

85
00:05:52,500 --> 00:05:54,580
Like, for idols?

86
00:05:54,580 --> 00:05:56,000
That's right.

87
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:58,250
You're the girl from earlier!

88
00:05:58,250 --> 00:06:01,000
So, you're going to become an idol?

89
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:03,000
It hasn't been decided yet.

90
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:05,830
The audition just ended.

91
00:06:05,830 --> 00:06:07,410
Audition...

92
00:06:07,410 --> 00:06:08,750
I see.

93
00:06:08,750 --> 00:06:12,250
I'm sorry, it was my misunderstanding.

94
00:06:12,250 --> 00:06:13,870
Come on, let's go.

95
00:06:13,870 --> 00:06:18,080
Actually... May I audition, too?

96
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:21,200
You're supposed to pass
a screening before that--

97
00:06:21,200 --> 00:06:22,200
You.

98
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:23,040
What's your name?

99
00:06:23,040 --> 00:06:24,040
Huh?

100
00:06:24,040 --> 00:06:25,250
What?

101
00:06:25,250 --> 00:06:26,910
It's Sakura Kawasaki.

102
00:06:26,910 --> 00:06:32,120
I'm able to tell what's important
and necessary for me.

103
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:34,330
What do you mean by that?

104
00:06:34,330 --> 00:06:36,750
My heart lets me know.

105
00:06:36,750 --> 00:06:39,540
It directs me to places and to take action.

106
00:06:39,540 --> 00:06:43,290
My heart's never let me down before.

107
00:06:43,290 --> 00:06:45,330
So, that's why you're here?

108
00:06:45,330 --> 00:06:46,660
Yes!

109
00:06:46,660 --> 00:06:50,870
My beating heart led me here
and I bumped into her.

110
00:06:50,870 --> 00:06:54,160
My heart hasn't stopped pounding ever since!

111
00:06:54,160 --> 00:06:56,500
It must be telling me to become an idol!

112
00:06:56,500 --> 00:06:57,870
You gotta be kidding me.

113
00:06:58,870 --> 00:07:04,370
You have no idea how many girls
are working hard to get into this world.

114
00:07:04,370 --> 00:07:08,620
You have no idea how many girls
can't even get a chance...

115
00:07:10,160 --> 00:07:13,450
This isn't a world you can enter
with such a ridiculous reason.

116
00:07:13,450 --> 00:07:17,540
It's not ridiculous. This is what I believe.

117
00:07:17,540 --> 00:07:19,790
I believe in my heart.

118
00:07:19,790 --> 00:07:23,370
As she said, the idol world is a severe place.

119
00:07:23,370 --> 00:07:28,120
Nowadays, your ability gets
quantified by the Venus Program.

120
00:07:28,120 --> 00:07:30,290
There's a clear split between
winners and losers,

121
00:07:30,290 --> 00:07:32,580
so you can say it's become
as harsh as ever.

122
00:07:32,580 --> 00:07:38,330
We're doing this audition to judge whether you
got what it takes to survive in such a world.

123
00:07:38,330 --> 00:07:42,830
Even if you sign with us, there's
no guarantee that you will succeed.

124
00:07:42,830 --> 00:07:45,200
Now, do you still want to audition?

125
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:46,870
Yes!

126
00:07:46,870 --> 00:07:48,580
So what can you do?

127
00:07:51,660 --> 00:07:53,450
I can sing!

128
00:07:53,450 --> 00:07:55,120
Will you sing for us now?

129
00:07:55,120 --> 00:07:56,250
Yes!

130
00:08:01,450 --> 00:08:05,700
♬ The story begins now ♬

131
00:08:05,700 --> 00:08:10,080
♬ Like dancing flower petals ♬

132
00:08:10,080 --> 00:08:18,700
♬ Let's hurry and run towards
the future with light steps! ♬

133
00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:22,950
♬ The glory I dreamed about ♬

134
00:08:22,950 --> 00:08:26,120
♬ In order to achieve it ♬

135
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:28,120
♬ I'll keep my face up ♬

136
00:08:28,120 --> 00:08:29,910
♬ Face forward ♬

137
00:08:29,910 --> 00:08:31,040
♬ Ready! ♬

138
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:35,540
♬ I make my wish through
this song and go forward ♬

139
00:08:35,540 --> 00:08:38,620
♬ First step ♬

140
00:08:41,790 --> 00:08:43,160
Oh my goodness.

141
00:08:43,160 --> 00:08:46,830
You sounded just like Mana.

142
00:08:46,830 --> 00:08:50,370
I wasn't good at singing when I was little.

143
00:08:50,370 --> 00:08:54,660
But one day, I woke up, being able to sing!

144
00:08:54,660 --> 00:08:56,450
Yeah, I know.

145
00:08:57,450 --> 00:09:00,040
Makino?

146
00:09:00,040 --> 00:09:03,500
Why did you run off like that earlier?

147
00:09:03,500 --> 00:09:06,620
Seeing Kotono surprised me.

148
00:09:06,620 --> 00:09:08,250
Still...

149
00:09:08,250 --> 00:09:10,120
I wasn't expecting it.

150
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:11,580
And...

151
00:09:11,580 --> 00:09:16,040
When I think about how much grief
I put her through...

152
00:09:16,040 --> 00:09:18,000
I felt too ashamed...

153
00:09:20,370 --> 00:09:24,580
But I never thought Kotono
would aim to become an idol.

154
00:09:24,580 --> 00:09:28,250
She's matured a lot since I last saw her, too.

155
00:09:28,250 --> 00:09:30,330
--But you came back to check on her anyway...

156
00:09:30,330 --> 00:09:31,500
--It's not like that.
--But you came back to check on her anyway...

157
00:09:32,500 --> 00:09:36,250
I wanted to leave Kotono up to you, Makino.

158
00:09:36,250 --> 00:09:38,580
But then I heard that girl's singing...

159
00:09:38,580 --> 00:09:40,290
Sakura Kawasaki's?

160
00:09:40,290 --> 00:09:43,410
Yup. It got me really curious...

161
00:09:43,410 --> 00:09:45,410
So I came back.

162
00:09:45,410 --> 00:09:48,910
I thought her singing sounded a lot like yours.

163
00:09:48,910 --> 00:09:52,080
Really? I can't tell myself.

164
00:09:53,910 --> 00:09:57,000
You knew about Kotono and didn't tell me.

165
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:00,330
You're the one who chose
not to look at the resumes.

166
00:10:00,330 --> 00:10:02,000
Still...

167
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:07,330
Mana's biological sister and a
mysterious girl with Mana's voice...

168
00:10:07,330 --> 00:10:08,700
So what's your verdict?

169
00:10:08,700 --> 00:10:13,370
I bet you're getting a kick
out of this, Mr. Saegusa.

170
00:10:13,370 --> 00:10:15,580
You're the one responsible.

171
00:10:15,580 --> 00:10:16,870
Yes.

172
00:10:20,370 --> 00:10:21,540
"Kotono Nagase
Confidential
Audition Results
DO NOT BEND"

173
00:10:21,540 --> 00:10:23,450
"Acceptance Letter
'Newcomer Discovery Project' Results
Thank you for applying to the
'Newcomer Discovery Project.'

174
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:35,500
Kotono!

175
00:10:39,290 --> 00:10:41,950
Looking forward to working with you!

176
00:10:41,950 --> 00:10:43,580
You, too.

177
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:47,000
<i>Idoly Pride.</i>

178
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:48,750
"Hoshimi Productions"

179
00:10:49,160 --> 00:10:52,500
I'm Kotono Nagase.
I look forward to working with you.

180
00:10:52,500 --> 00:10:55,950
I'm Sakura Kawasaki.
I look forward to working with you!

181
00:10:55,950 --> 00:10:58,370
Makino is in charge of both of you.

182
00:10:58,370 --> 00:11:03,370
There will be many challenges ahead, but I hope
to work hard and conquer them together.

183
00:11:03,370 --> 00:11:04,750
Welcome aboard.

184
00:11:04,750 --> 00:11:05,750
Thank you!

185
00:11:07,250 --> 00:11:11,370
Makino used to be Mana's assistant manager.

186
00:11:11,370 --> 00:11:12,580
What?

187
00:11:12,580 --> 00:11:16,370
Mana's the one who brought Makino here, right?

188
00:11:16,370 --> 00:11:17,870
She did?

189
00:11:17,870 --> 00:11:20,040
Well, it's a long story...

190
00:11:20,040 --> 00:11:24,870
It just so happened that we sat next to
each other in class, so it was easy to ask.

191
00:11:24,870 --> 00:11:28,790
Um... Kotono's sister... Is it by any chance...?

192
00:11:28,790 --> 00:11:31,620
Yeah, I'll explain later.

193
00:11:31,620 --> 00:11:34,120
Now, I'll give you both a tour of the office.

194
00:11:34,120 --> 00:11:35,580
You can leave your things there.

195
00:11:35,580 --> 00:11:37,160
Okay!

196
00:11:51,750 --> 00:11:53,500
So that's the story.

197
00:11:53,500 --> 00:11:55,950
Kotono is Mana's...!

198
00:11:55,950 --> 00:11:59,870
Anyway, I heard about your
health condition from your parents...

199
00:11:59,870 --> 00:12:01,120
Yes.

200
00:12:15,160 --> 00:12:16,330
I give up!

201
00:12:20,580 --> 00:12:22,750
I'm no good at all.

202
00:12:22,750 --> 00:12:25,500
You never break out of the pose.
It's impressive, Kotono!

203
00:12:25,500 --> 00:12:28,080
I do basic training regularly.

204
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:29,580
I see!

205
00:12:29,580 --> 00:12:31,910
As for me...

206
00:12:31,910 --> 00:12:34,950
I was never the athletic type.

207
00:12:34,950 --> 00:12:37,540
Do you think you can really make it like that?

208
00:12:37,540 --> 00:12:38,540
Yup!

209
00:12:38,540 --> 00:12:42,120
I believe in what I felt in my heart that day.

210
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:46,830
Did they tell you about me?

211
00:12:46,830 --> 00:12:49,700
Yup, from Mr. Makino.

212
00:12:49,700 --> 00:12:51,000
What did you think?

213
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,120
I was surprised!

214
00:12:52,120 --> 00:12:54,200
Kotono, you're the Mana Nagase--

215
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:57,000
I mean, Miss Mana's little sister.

216
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:01,370
Even I know who she is, when I
don't know much about idols.

217
00:13:01,370 --> 00:13:05,160
You sang my sister's song at the audition.

218
00:13:05,160 --> 00:13:07,950
Yup! I really like that song.

219
00:13:07,950 --> 00:13:12,290
But what a coincidence that this was her agency!

220
00:13:13,330 --> 00:13:18,410
If we were to make our debut,
does that make us Miss Mana's juniors?

221
00:13:19,500 --> 00:13:22,370
She's not here anymore.

222
00:13:22,370 --> 00:13:24,410
Kotono...

223
00:13:24,410 --> 00:13:27,580
Your regular lessons will start tomorrow.

224
00:13:27,580 --> 00:13:28,410
Yes!

225
00:13:28,410 --> 00:13:33,450
And you'll be moving into the dorms soon,
so be prepared.

226
00:13:33,450 --> 00:13:34,750
Understood!

227
00:13:34,750 --> 00:13:38,250
You'll meet the other members soon, too.

228
00:13:38,250 --> 00:13:39,830
I can't wait!

229
00:13:40,910 --> 00:13:43,580
Thank you for today!

230
00:13:43,580 --> 00:13:47,080
I'm so curious about the other members!

231
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:48,790
Aren't you?

232
00:13:48,790 --> 00:13:49,950
Not really.

233
00:13:49,950 --> 00:13:53,120
I wanted to be a solo artist originally.

234
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:54,250
I see.

235
00:13:54,250 --> 00:13:56,160
Miss Mana was, too, right?

236
00:14:02,580 --> 00:14:03,910
Hey, Big Sister...

237
00:14:03,910 --> 00:14:05,660
Who are they?

238
00:14:07,700 --> 00:14:09,540
Big Sister...?

239
00:14:11,080 --> 00:14:15,410
I've decided that I want to be in the industry,
become an idol!

240
00:14:15,410 --> 00:14:17,580
That came out of nowhere.

241
00:14:17,580 --> 00:14:19,370
It can't be that easy to be--

242
00:14:19,370 --> 00:14:20,700
Sure it is!

243
00:14:20,700 --> 00:14:24,250
I was scouted by a famous
producer the other day!

244
00:14:25,250 --> 00:14:26,750
I'm home.

245
00:14:26,750 --> 00:14:28,450
Where's Big Sister?

246
00:14:28,450 --> 00:14:31,250
She said it's another late night at work.

247
00:14:35,080 --> 00:14:36,620
What? Kotono said that?

248
00:14:36,620 --> 00:14:40,080
She thinks your work is getting between you two.

249
00:14:42,250 --> 00:14:45,040
Will you come see my performance
at the finals tomorrow?

250
00:14:45,040 --> 00:14:47,700
You want me to witness your victory?

251
00:14:47,700 --> 00:14:51,830
No, there's a song I want you to hear.

252
00:14:55,250 --> 00:14:57,450
Since you became an idol,

253
00:14:57,450 --> 00:14:59,750
it's been such a nuisance for me.

254
00:14:59,750 --> 00:15:02,160
All they talk about at school is you.

255
00:15:02,160 --> 00:15:06,250
People hassle me for your autograph
or a chance to meet you...

256
00:15:06,250 --> 00:15:08,910
--Sorry.
--Don't apologize.

257
00:15:10,790 --> 00:15:12,750
If this were the case...

258
00:15:26,950 --> 00:15:29,370
Yes, this is Nagase.

259
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:34,750
Yes... Yes, I'm her younger sister.

260
00:15:39,700 --> 00:15:40,910
What...?

261
00:15:52,500 --> 00:15:54,040
A diary...?

262
00:16:02,790 --> 00:16:04,370
Big Sister...

263
00:16:06,910 --> 00:16:08,290
Kotono!

264
00:16:09,410 --> 00:16:11,950
See you later! I'm this way!

265
00:16:11,950 --> 00:16:14,200
Can't wait for tomorrow!

266
00:16:15,160 --> 00:16:17,830
You don't want me to tell your sister?

267
00:16:17,830 --> 00:16:18,910
What?

268
00:16:18,910 --> 00:16:24,540
"Your sister has unfinished business,
so she's still lingering around as a ghost"?

269
00:16:24,540 --> 00:16:27,200
I would word it a little differently...

270
00:16:27,200 --> 00:16:29,830
There's no way you could tell her.

271
00:16:29,830 --> 00:16:33,910
Kotono's probably trying
to become an idol for me.

272
00:16:33,910 --> 00:16:38,790
She's trying to achieve the thing I left undone.

273
00:16:38,790 --> 00:16:41,450
If Kotono's the one who'll take over my dream...

274
00:16:41,450 --> 00:16:43,500
I can never be happier.

275
00:16:43,500 --> 00:16:44,700
Mana...

276
00:16:44,700 --> 00:16:48,870
Since I disappeared,
she got motivated to do this.

277
00:16:48,870 --> 00:16:50,370
That's why...

278
00:16:50,370 --> 00:16:55,500
If she actualizes my dream for me,
maybe I can finally rest in peace.

279
00:16:55,790 --> 00:16:57,540
"Hoshimi Productions"

280
00:16:57,830 --> 00:16:59,750
Field training?

281
00:16:59,750 --> 00:17:01,790
Yeah, go get ready.

282
00:17:04,950 --> 00:17:07,000
In front of the train station...?

283
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:08,370
That's right.

284
00:17:08,370 --> 00:17:09,700
This place...

285
00:17:09,700 --> 00:17:11,200
Let's try singing here.

286
00:17:11,200 --> 00:17:13,080
What? But there's people around...

287
00:17:13,080 --> 00:17:16,000
You'll eventually sing in front
of even more people.

288
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:17,660
It's better to get used to that now.

289
00:17:17,660 --> 00:17:21,660
But singing on stage and
singing at a place like this is--

290
00:17:21,660 --> 00:17:22,830
The same.

291
00:17:22,830 --> 00:17:25,540
The stage isn't something that's provided.

292
00:17:25,540 --> 00:17:28,660
Wherever you sing becomes the stage.

293
00:17:30,120 --> 00:17:36,000
This is the place where a certain idol
often came to practice singing.

294
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:37,910
Could that "certain idol" be...?

295
00:17:37,910 --> 00:17:39,000
I'll do it.

296
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:40,500
Kotono?!

297
00:17:40,500 --> 00:17:42,750
I would watch her, too, sometimes.

298
00:17:42,750 --> 00:17:45,870
My sister singing here...

299
00:17:47,660 --> 00:17:50,040
All right, so let's get singing.

300
00:17:50,040 --> 00:17:51,750
I'll be watching from over there.

301
00:17:51,750 --> 00:17:54,540
What?! Um... Mr. Makino...

302
00:17:57,250 --> 00:17:59,330
Sakura, are you ready?

303
00:17:59,330 --> 00:18:00,750
Y-Yeah!

304
00:18:05,660 --> 00:18:11,660
♬ I've encountered something I love
from the bottom of my heart ♬

305
00:18:11,660 --> 00:18:14,040
♬ For the very first time ♬

306
00:18:14,040 --> 00:18:18,160
♬ This racing heart isn't a coincidence ♬

307
00:18:18,160 --> 00:18:22,370
♬ It's a sign I chose the right path ♬

308
00:18:22,370 --> 00:18:26,750
♬ A healing sakura-colored wind ♬

309
00:18:26,750 --> 00:18:31,040
♬ Encourages me to push forward ♬

310
00:18:31,040 --> 00:18:33,200
♬ An unknown path ♬

311
00:18:33,200 --> 00:18:34,700
♬ I wonder what awaits ♬

312
00:18:34,700 --> 00:18:40,540
♬ I'm filled with a fluttering sensation ♬

313
00:18:40,540 --> 00:18:42,290
Kotono...

314
00:18:42,290 --> 00:18:46,620
♬ The story begins now ♬

315
00:18:46,620 --> 00:18:50,870
♬ Like dancing flower petals ♬

316
00:18:50,870 --> 00:18:51,700
--♬ Let's hurry and run towards
the future with light steps! ♬

317
00:18:51,700 --> 00:18:55,450
--Sakura's voice... It really sounds like her.
--♬ Let's hurry and run towards
the future with light steps! ♬

318
00:18:55,450 --> 00:18:59,410
--♬ Let's hurry and run towards
the future with light steps! ♬

319
00:18:59,410 --> 00:19:03,870
♬ The glory I dreamed about ♬

320
00:19:03,870 --> 00:19:06,870
♬ In order to achieve it ♬

321
00:19:06,870 --> 00:19:09,250
♬ I'll keep my face up ♬

322
00:19:09,250 --> 00:19:10,830
♬ Face forward ♬

323
00:19:10,830 --> 00:19:11,910
♬ Ready! ♬

324
00:19:11,910 --> 00:19:16,450
♬ I make my wish through this song
and go forward ♬

325
00:19:16,450 --> 00:19:19,500
♬ First step! ♬

326
00:19:20,540 --> 00:19:22,540
Wow!

327
00:19:22,540 --> 00:19:24,660
--They remind me of Mana.
--Yeah!

328
00:19:24,660 --> 00:19:27,120
People called her "that girl after school."

329
00:19:27,120 --> 00:19:30,330
You look just like Mana.

330
00:19:30,330 --> 00:19:31,790
Y-Yes.

331
00:19:31,790 --> 00:19:32,870
I'm her sister.

332
00:19:32,870 --> 00:19:34,290
Oh, really?

333
00:19:34,290 --> 00:19:38,290
Your singing makes me think of Mana.

334
00:19:38,290 --> 00:19:39,330
What?

335
00:19:39,330 --> 00:19:41,790
Best of luck to you both!

336
00:19:43,040 --> 00:19:46,200
Thank you very much!

337
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:50,000
Does my singing really sound like Miss Mana's?

338
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:52,290
You're not trying to imitate her?

339
00:19:52,290 --> 00:19:56,450
I would listen to her songs, but I never
intentionally tried to sound like her.

340
00:19:57,620 --> 00:19:59,290
You do sound like her.

341
00:19:59,290 --> 00:20:01,910
It's the color... or the feel of your voice.

342
00:20:01,910 --> 00:20:04,540
Even I think so, as her sister.

343
00:20:04,540 --> 00:20:06,370
Really...

344
00:20:08,910 --> 00:20:10,870
Wow, it's big!

345
00:20:10,870 --> 00:20:13,620
It used to be some kind of recreation facility.

346
00:20:13,620 --> 00:20:16,000
Your things should be delivered already.

347
00:20:17,200 --> 00:20:18,910
Oh, Mr. Makino.

348
00:20:18,910 --> 00:20:20,580
Are they...?

349
00:20:20,580 --> 00:20:24,040
I want to introduce them,
so let's gather in the living room.

350
00:20:25,830 --> 00:20:27,250
I'm Saki Shiraishi.

351
00:20:27,250 --> 00:20:28,950
A third-year in high school.

352
00:20:28,950 --> 00:20:32,450
I'm probably the eldest of the members.

353
00:20:32,450 --> 00:20:34,540
I'm her sister, Chisa Shiraishi.

354
00:20:34,540 --> 00:20:36,160
It's nice to meet you.

355
00:20:36,160 --> 00:20:38,250
I am the one and only Suzu Narumiya.

356
00:20:38,250 --> 00:20:41,700
The name Narumiya probably rung a bell for you.

357
00:20:41,700 --> 00:20:45,790
I am <i>the </i>daughter of the
prestigious Narumiya family.

358
00:20:48,700 --> 00:20:51,870
What is with the pathetic reaction?!

359
00:20:51,870 --> 00:20:54,790
You can be a little more impressed, you know?!

360
00:20:54,790 --> 00:20:57,450
Miss Saki seems more high-class to me.

361
00:20:57,450 --> 00:20:59,450
I heard that!

362
00:20:59,450 --> 00:21:01,250
I'm Shizuku Hyodo.

363
00:21:02,540 --> 00:21:05,080
I'm Sakura Kawasaki, nice to meet you.

364
00:21:05,080 --> 00:21:06,790
I'm Kotono Nagase.

365
00:21:06,790 --> 00:21:08,950
Nagase? Are you...?

366
00:21:08,950 --> 00:21:10,080
I'm her sister.

367
00:21:10,080 --> 00:21:11,700
I see.

368
00:21:11,700 --> 00:21:13,250
You look like her.

369
00:21:13,250 --> 00:21:15,500
Huh? What is it?

370
00:21:15,500 --> 00:21:17,700
Go ahead and pick an open room.

371
00:21:17,700 --> 00:21:20,250
The room next to me should be open, too.

372
00:21:25,370 --> 00:21:26,200
What's the matter?

373
00:21:26,200 --> 00:21:29,500
Um... Mr. Makino, will you be staying here, too?

374
00:21:29,500 --> 00:21:33,830
Yeah, I moved here a little while ago
as sort of a supervisor...

375
00:21:33,830 --> 00:21:35,950
All girls can be a little--

376
00:21:35,950 --> 00:21:37,950
Um... What's wrong?

377
00:21:41,950 --> 00:21:43,200
Huh?

378
00:21:45,540 --> 00:21:48,660
Why do I have to stay in a shed?

379
00:21:48,660 --> 00:21:50,290
Well, of course!

380
00:21:50,290 --> 00:21:52,660
And plus it suits you, Makino.

381
00:21:52,660 --> 00:21:54,120
What does that mean?

382
00:21:54,120 --> 00:21:57,790
Don't worry, I'll watch over
the girls in the dorm.

383
00:21:57,790 --> 00:21:59,870
I don't get it.

384
00:21:59,870 --> 00:22:02,700
It seems like it'll be lively
and fun around here.

385
00:22:05,120 --> 00:22:07,830
Huh?! What is this?! How do I stop it?

386
00:22:07,830 --> 00:22:09,500
What?! Oh, no!

387
00:22:09,500 --> 00:22:12,620
Wait! W-W-Wait a minute! Hold on! Please!

388
00:22:12,620 --> 00:22:13,040
K-Kotono! Help me!

389
00:22:13,040 --> 00:22:17,040
"The Reason We Stand Here"

390
00:22:13,040 --> 00:22:17,040
K-Kotono! Help me!

